course: dictionary
lesson: 16059
title: A sound made with the voice
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A formal word can sound hard, but it often hides a simple idea. Look at the word parts: vocal is about the voice, and the ending -isation turns it into a noun, a thing you can name. «The whale's vocalisation carried across the ocean.» The sound came from the whale's voice, so vocalisation must mean a sound made with the voice.
explain: Scientists use this word when they study how animals talk to each other. «Scientists recorded the monkeys' vocalisations in the forest.» The clue is recorded: you record sounds, not pictures or food. A bark, a howl, a birdsong and a call are all vocalisations.
explain: Musicians also use the word. «The choir began with a vocalisation on the sounds "ah" and "oh", with no words at all.» Here it means singing a tune on vowel sounds. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: "a sound made with the voice" still makes sense, so you have understood it.
fact: Vocalisation means a sound made with the voice.
fact: Animals such as whales, birds and monkeys make vocalisations to communicate.
fact: In music, a vocalisation is a tune sung on vowel sounds, without words.
fact: «Vocalisation» means the act of making sounds with the voice or of singing.
fact: The word has vocal inside it, which has to do with the voice; the ending -isation makes it a noun.
exercise: «The whale's vocalisation carried across the ocean.» What is a vocalisation? | A deep dive into cold water | A tail movement used to swim | A map of the sea floor | *A sound made with the voice
exercise: «Scientists recorded the monkeys' vocalisations in the forest.» Find and copy the word that names the sounds. | *vocalisations | scientists | forest | recorded
exercise: In music, what is a vocalisation? | *Singing a tune on vowel sounds without words | Writing a song down on paper | Playing a tune on a piano | Clapping along to the beat
test: A bird's call and a dog's bark are both examples of what? | rainbows | castles | sunsets | *vocalisations
test: Vocalisation is a formal word. What does it mean in plain English? | A type of tall building | A way to write in code | *A sound made with the voice | A kind of cloud
exam: In «Scientists recorded the monkeys' vocalisations in the forest», what were the scientists recording? | The weather in the forest | *The sounds the monkeys make with their voices | Bananas and fruit | The trees' shadows
